<title>FRANCE: Algerian leading bank increases capital.</title>
<headline>Algerian leading bank increases capital.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's leading bank Credit Populaire d'Algerie has increased its capital by 46 percent to 13.6 billion dinars ($247 million), the official APS news agency said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The bank's capital was 9.3 billion dinars in 1995, the agency said.</p>
<p>Established in Algiers in 1966, the Credit Populaire d'Algerie posted a net profit of 378.8 million dinars in 1995, it said.</p>
<p>The bank has stakes in 10 enterprises including the Algerian-Moroccan Meditrade.</p>
<p>($1= 55 dinars)</p>
</text>
